  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Core Task**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the fundamental user request: crafting a `/plan` for a browser extension. The key functionality revolves around exporting billing statement CSVs from various financial websites and seamlessly saving them to a cloud storage service, such as Google Drive. I am organizing the extension into folders.\n\n\n**Refining the Extension Goal**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how to handle the CSV files. Specifically, each user-added extractor will involve a dedicated folder named after the financial institution. I am thinking about how to best represent the final desired `/plan`: a plan, or an implementation prototype? I\'ve confirmed that I cannot directly build the browser extension itself in this environment, but I *can* create an app that outputs the extension scaffold or a demo UI as a starting point. This resolves the implementation constraint.\n\n\n**Clarifying Delivery Method**\n\nI\'m now determining the optimal delivery for this `/plan`. While a detailed Markdown plan in the chat is essential, I believe adding a minimal extension scaffold would be helpful. However, the core of the request is for a comprehensive plan in the `/plan` format, and I will focus on that. I\'ll provide an explanation of architecture for the extension, and ask if a functional UI mockup of the popup is desired.\n\n\n**Designing the Dashboard**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a web-based companion React app. I envision it acting as a \"Project Plan & Architecture\" dashboard. This will elegantly display the proposed extension structure, its technical components, and a step-by-step implementation guide for building the browser extension. The app\'s dashboard will act as a control center.\n\n\n**Defining the Upload Process**\n\nI\'m now detailing the CSV upload procedure. The extension will intercept the user\'s initiated CSV download, read the file, and authenticate with the Google Drive API. Then, it will locate or create a dedicated folder for the financial institution and save the CSV with a standardized name.\n\nI\'m leaning towards providing a React-based UI mockup of the extension popup, rather than building the entire scaffold, and the plan, in Chinese, as requested, to give a tangible starting point. Finally, I will update the `metadata.json` as a deliverable.\n\n\n**Constructing the UI Mockup**\n\nI\'m currently building the `App.tsx` mockup for the Extension Popup, sized 350x500px, centered. This mockup will include settings and a simulated \"Syncing\" state to visualize the user experience. I am updating the `metadata.json` and creating the `ExtensionMockup.tsx` and `PlanDocument.tsx` components. Then, I plan to modify `App.tsx` to display both the plan and the mockup. The plan details focus on the UI (React + Tailwind), Content Script (strategy-pattern-based parsers), and Background Script (Google Drive API authorization).\n\n\n**Addressing Technical Challenges**\n\nI am now focusing on the technical hurdles. I\'ve pinpointed the challenges, mainly around data acquisition (direct downloads versus dynamic table parsing), Google Drive API integration, and multi-institution adaptability, with potential for config driven parsers. I am now planning steps: manifest v3, Google Drive OAuth integration, 1-2 banks for MVP.\nI will also need to re-think how I draft the `App.tsx` layout.\nI am now finalizing the file naming convention, too.\n\n\n**Refining the UI Components**\n\nI am now focusing on the components of the user interface mockup, particularly the icons from `lucide-react`. I\'ve started by updating `metadata.json` to reflect the project\'s name and description. Now, I am structuring the `App.tsx` file for a 320x480 container. I\'ve considered including the plan information in Chinese within a dedicated section, alongside the extension mockup. I will now create components for plan and mockup.\n\n\n**Crafting the Extension Mockup**\n\nI\'m presently building the extension\'s UI mockup, now including a dedicated section for the plan documentation. I\'m focusing on incorporating Chinese text, as requested, within the interface. I\'m incorporating Tailwind for polished styling, and considering adding `motion` for visual enhancements. The mockup will feature a \"Statement Sync\" header, Drive status, and list detected banks and files. The plan will be presented in Chinese with sections for architecture, modules, tech challenges, and roadmap.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Chinese Plan**\n\nI\'m now integrating the Chinese plan text within the React mockup\'s dedicated section. I\'ve focused on ensuring the text\'s clarity and readability. I am also working on styling to present the plan components effectively and ensuring the visual layout is clean and user-friendly.\n\n\n\n**Clarifying Execution Constraints**\n\nI\'m now clarifying the delivery format to indicate that the system cannot directly generate a built extension, but the React code is available. I\'ll need to modify the UI mockup to clarify that it\'s a demonstration, and I\'ll make sure to mention that the user can start implementing the actual extension codebase using that code. I\'m also planning to extract components from `App.tsx` for cleaner code and planning to edit the `/metadata.json` and `/src/App.tsx`, create `/src/components/PlanDocument.tsx` and `/src/components/ExtensionPopupMockup.tsx` files. I will have to find out if the parent directory already exists.\n\n\n**Finalizing the File Creation**\n\nI\'m now implementing the plan by creating and editing files based on the structure outlined. I\'ve focused on `PlanDocument.tsx` and `ExtensionPopupMockup.tsx`. I am ensuring proper integration and ensuring that the content displays according to the plan. Next, I will populate the JSX content within the mockups for `PlanDocument.tsx` and `ExtensionPopupMockup.tsx` and integrate the components to the `App.tsx` file, along with file creation details in `/metadata.json`.\n\n\n**Implementing Parallel Actions**\n\nI\'m now structuring the planned file operations to execute concurrently. I\'ll utilize tool calls for parallel execution, specifically creating `/src/components/PlanDocument.tsx` and `/src/components/ExtensionPopupMockup.tsx`, and editing `/src/App.tsx` and `/metadata.json`. I\'ve confirmed `lucide-react` is already a dependency.\nI\'m drafting the `PlanDocument.tsx` with `lucide-react` imports.\n\n\n\n**Describing the Chinese Plan**\n\nI\'m now integrating the Chinese text into the mockup UI. I\'m focusing on ensuring clear and readable Chinese text within a user-friendly layout. I\'m finalizing the structure for presentation of the plan\'s components. I\'ve focused on styling that is clean and user-friendly for the plan and the mockup.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Workflow**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"Data Extraction\" workflow, focusing on DOM parsing or download interception based on bank-specific needs (Chase, BoA, etc.). I\'m finalizing the structure to describe the architecture and the core business flow, and I am preparing the `PlanDocument.tsx` with all the sections.\n\nI will also finalize the content for the `Background Service Worker` and ensure that it can handle the Google Drive OAuth, create institution folders, and upload the CSV files.\n\n\n**Refining the Parsing Strategy**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on data acquisition. I\'ll utilize a strategy pattern to map URLs to parsers. It could be parsing data from DOM tables or capturing the official CSV download. I am also working on standardizing the format to `[institution]_[account_number]_[date].csv`.\n\nI am also making sure that the final plan will outline how to utilize a Background Service Worker to handle Google Drive OAuth, creating institution folders, and uploading CSVs.\n\n\n**Detailing the Upload Process**\n\nI\'m now implementing the Google Drive API call. I\'m focusing on handling folder existence before uploading the CSV. If no folder for the bank exists, I\'ll create one. I will upload the CSV file inside. This completes section 2 for the `/PlanDocument.tsx`.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Plan Document**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided Chinese text and styling it, to make the documentation readable. I am preparing the content for `PlanDocument.tsx`, including all plan sections. I\'ll finalize the \"Data Extraction\" workflow to present in the plan.\n\nI am also making sure that the final plan will outline how to utilize a Background Service Worker to handle Google Drive OAuth, creating institution folders, and uploading CSVs.\n\n\n**Simulating the Sync Process**\n\nI\'m now integrating the UI for handling the sync operation. I\'ve built a simulated syncing state with the use of `setIsSyncing` and `setSynced`. I will use Tailwind to add visual cues for processing and completion states within the extension. I am planning to represent states in React components to emulate the user experience when syncing.\n\n\n\n**Visualizing the Sync Process**\n\nI\'m now focused on the visual cues for the syncing operation within the mockup, using Tailwind. I\'ve successfully incorporated simulated states to represent processing and completion for a user-friendly experience. I am now aiming to incorporate more detailed visual feedback on the state of the sync within the extension.\n\n\n**Visualizing the Sync Process**\n\nI\'m now adding more visual enhancements to the sync process, still using Tailwind. I\'m focusing on providing clear visual feedback, including success and error states. I am now updating the mock extension\'s user interface.\n\n\n\n**Visualizing the File List**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided code block within the extension mockup to show a list of files that have been processed. I will ensure that the integration is aligned with the overall UI design. I\'m focusing on the implementation of a scrollable section, using the `className` properties provided in the code.\n\nI\'m now also including a \"Drive\" section with file icons and metadata to display a list of files. This shows the Drive with its files.\n\n\n**Confirming Requirements Compliance**\n\nI\'m now confirming the plan\'s alignment with the initial request. I\'m providing a comprehensive plan detailed in the React UI and a corresponding extension popup mockup to guide implementation. I will prepare a Chinese summary, and that can complete the response to the user.\n\n\n**Defining Implementation Actions**\n\nI\'m now detailing the file operations. I\'ll create `PlanDocument.tsx` and `ExtensionPopupMockup.tsx`. I will overwrite `App.tsx` and `metadata.json` with the new content, per the specifications for file manipulation. I\'ve re-reviewed the tool documentation and file structures.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 64
