    thinking: "**Understanding OAuth Flow**\n\nI\'ve been examining how `set_up_oauth` in AI Studio manages Firebase Authentication to acquire an OAuth access token. I now see this token is then used to call Google APIs. My understanding is expanding to consider this within the context of a Chrome extension mockup.\n\n\n**Analyzing Chrome Extension OAuth**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the Chrome extension\'s OAuth implementation. The `background.ts` script uses `chrome.identity.getAuthToken`, which is standard. The `manifest.json` file confirms the use of OAuth2 with the specified client ID and scopes. The user wants me to implement this flow for Google Drive access, which is already present but maybe the UI/UX? I\'m re-examining the potential need to manage token caching and removal to meet the user\'s need.\n\n\n**Implementing Folder Creation Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the folder creation requirement. I need to add `findOrCreateFolder(token, folderName)` to `background.ts`. This function will check for or create folders based on the institution\'s name, as specified by the user. I\'m also considering a \"Connect to Drive\" button in the popup to trigger the authentication flow using `chrome.identity.getAuthToken`. This button will handle the OAuth flow within the popup itself, connecting to the user\'s Drive and handling token management.\n\n\n**Refining File Upload**\n\nI\'m now refining the `handleDriveUpload` function in `background.ts`. It will accept the `folderName` directly, which simplifies the process. I\'m also actively implementing `findOrCreateFolder` within `background.ts` to manage folder interactions. This new function searches for or creates folders, based on the provided name.\n\n\n**Clarifying File Access**\n\nI\'ve just realized a critical detail about the OAuth scope: `\"https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file\"` limits the extension to files/folders it *creates*. This means the folder search logic is essential, as the extension only \"sees\" its own. The existing search logic within `findOrCreateFolder` is now confirmed as vital!\n\n\n**Refining OAuth Integration**\n\nI\'m now revising my approach to ensure robust OAuth integration with the Drive API. I\'ve updated the `uploadCsvToDrive` function to accept a `folderId` parameter for enhanced control over file placement. This change allows me to directly specify the target folder for uploads. I\'m also implementing a mechanism within the popup to check authentication status. I\'m using `chrome.identity.getAuthToken({ interactive: false })` in the background script and message listeners for `CHECK_AUTH` and `LOGIN`.\n\n\n**Implementing Authentication Check**\n\nI\'m now integrating authentication status checks. I\'m using `chrome.identity.getAuthToken` with `interactive: false` to silently check if a token exists and `interactive: true` for user login. The `background.ts` script uses message listeners to handle `CHECK_AUTH` and `LOGIN` requests, sending back authentication status or initiating the login flow. I\'m also ensuring the correct folder name, \"Amex JP\", is returned.\n\n\n**Enhancing Popup UX**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the popup\'s user experience. I\'m adding an account status section with an indication of Drive connection status. The popup also contains a \"Connect\" button that triggers the OAuth flow. I\'m implementing the `handleLogin` function in `ExtensionPopupMockup.tsx` to handle this.\n\n\n"
