  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Error Messages**\n\nI\'ve been examining the error message block closely. Currently, I\'m focusing on refining its visual presentation and ensuring it\'s both informative and unobtrusive. The goal is to balance clarity with a design that doesn\'t detract from the user interface. I\'m exploring different ways to highlight the error without being overly jarring.\n\n\n**Implementing Toast Notifications**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to implementing a toast notification system as requested, replacing the inline error block. I\'m removing the old method and building a system that provides real-time feedback. I plan to use a new state variable to manage the toast messages and types. Successful uploads will trigger a success toast, and errors will trigger an error toast. I\'ve begun to create a showToast function to manage the toast state.\n\n\n**Refining Toast State**\n\nI\'m now refining the toast state management. I\'ve switched from a simple string error to a more structured state object containing both message and type (\'success\' or \'error\'). The `showToast` function is complete, handling the toast display and auto-hiding after three seconds. I\'ve updated both the `handleLogin` and `handleSync` functions to use the new `showToast` function. I\'m focusing on ensuring consistent and appropriate toast triggers in different scenarios.\n\n\n**Handling Upload Feedback**\n\nI\'m now focused on refining the upload success and failure notifications within the `handleSync` function. I\'ve integrated `chrome.runtime.sendMessage` to handle uploads to Google Drive. Based on the upload response, I\'m setting appropriate toast messages and managing the syncing state. I\'ve also added a try/catch block to cover any unexpected errors during the upload process, which will trigger an error toast.\n\n\n**Positioning Toast Notifications**\n\nI\'m now integrating the toast notification into the UI, placing it absolutely positioned at the bottom of the popup. I\'ve chosen to use Tailwind classes for animation, specifically `animate-in slide-in-from-bottom-2 fade-in`, to keep it simple if the `motion` library is not available. The plan is to ensure it visually complements the interface and provides a clear user experience.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 416717222
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
